sequenceDiagram
  %% Container runtime (ADR 0250 step 8, docs/reference/development-containers.md#migrate-a-checkout-instance): one checkout Instance moves into a container, with its code. Its database stays where it is, and the container gets its own way to it. A default Instance moves before the other Instances of its Project, and keeps its checkout until its last worktree has moved. The command exists only until the last checkout Instance has moved (docs/reference/old-paths.md). The container steps are the phases of docs/cli/instance/container/create-default.mmd and create.mmd.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:migrate
  %% kind: instance.migrate
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane C icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant C as New container<br/>via incus exec
  CLI->>GW: instance:migrate 42
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:migrate INSTANCE`
  %%> - syntax: `<instance> [--force] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  Note over CLI: Confirm the downtime
  %%> What it asks:
  %%> - the Instance goes down during the move, and its old checkout moves to retention after it; `--force` answers yes
  Note over GW: Validate, reserve runtime<br/>address · T3 port
  %%> If it never starts:
  %%> - cancellation or admission expiry frees the new reservation and releases deferred Schedule fires under the Instance lock; an uncertain start keeps its reservation
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the Instance is an active checkout Instance on an `app-dev` Node of the build list, else `instance.migrate_unsupported`
  %%> - a non-default Instance needs its Project's default Instance in a container first, else `instance.default_not_migrated`
  %%> - the Instance has only ordinary systemd or supported `vp-dev` Processes, no unfinished deployment or Process operation/runtime cleanup and no Route beside its own; a non-default Instance needs Conn and the model router, as a clone does
  %%> - `vp-dev` keeps its identity, assigned port and desired state; unsupported preset versions, custom commands, external paths and recorded container port conflicts refuse before downtime, naming the Process and reason
  %%> - a web-serving Project names its PHP version; a missing version refuses with `project.source_defaults_incomplete`, naming `orbit project:update PROJECT --source-access=github_app` to record it from source
  %%> - a database on a Database server has an IPv4 address and a port, else `instance.database_clone_unsupported`
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the runtime reservation records its owning Operation; late receipts cannot change a newer owner
  %%> - the whole-run budget is 5,100 seconds; a lower-bound test includes declared child, restoration and cleanup timeouts
  %%> - maps only known host command locations, preserving opaque env/shell strings, and records each Process/from/to translation in the terminal receipt
  %%> - the runtime record is reserved: the next bridge address and, for a non-default Instance, the lowest free T3 port
  %%> - the checkout stays the Instance's runtime until the Route has moved; the Route's Node is held for the run
  %%> - the Instance takes no deployment and no wake while the run lasts
  %%> - a non-default Instance's placeholder model key goes to the vault
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-migrate
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
  SW->>N: Launch, probe container<br/>Ansible · tags container
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - before any Node change, checks the recorded branch and every planned retirement; a refusal leaves prior resources untouched
  %%> - checks checkout symlinks and dependency package links before creating the container, skipping `.git` and installed package contents; broken links or targets outside the checkout refuse with `instance.migrate_symlink_unsupported`, naming every path and target
  %%> - retirement preflight refuses unpushed local branches or detached HEAD and stashes, with their existing named errors; it reads local refs only
  %%> - checks service hosts selected by cache, session, queue, broadcasting, database or mail drivers (never by Redis client or endpoint declarations alone) in the checkout and nested app `.env` files before any probe or Node change; direct services require an exact endpoint from the shared container access plan; unsupported endpoints refuse with `instance.migrate_env_service_unreachable`, naming the file, key and host:port without credentials; unreadable syntax names only the file and line, and traversal/read failures name only the path
  %%> - deletes a container that an earlier failed move left, then creates and starts the new container through the shared container phase; discard leaves shared bridge endpoint rules for host reconciliation
  %%> - each attached target gets an exact TCP allow in both the bridge and NIC ACLs; both keep default reject. Endpoint adds reread on ETag conflict, at most five attempts with a one-second delay
  %%> - probes every attached target from inside the container before downtime, else `instance.database_unreachable`
  %%> - checks mapped Process executables inside the container, then repeats before quiesce; unavailable paths report `instance.migrate_process_binary_unavailable` naming every Process and path, leaving the checkout serving
  %%> - fetches the branch from the checkout into the Node's mirror, including commits never pushed
  SW->>N: Check and stop<br/>Ansible · tags quiesce
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - repeats the branch and retirement checks
  %%> - checks every registered Node-timer Schedule and captures timer activation before stopping any writer; unsupported Schedules refuse with their name and reason
  %%> - repeats source symlink and environment checks before stopping any writer
  %%> - stops and disables host Schedule timers and Process units, then removes the awake marker
  %%> - records that quiesce began, so a failure before it never restarts host units or rewrites the awake marker
  SW->>C: Build the workspace<br/>Ansible · tags workspace
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - pushes the branch in as a bundle and checks it out in a standalone repository in `/srv/workspace`
  %%> - a non-default checkout is a linked worktree, so its `.git` is never copied
  SW->>C: Copy the files<br/>Ansible · tags files
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - copies every file that differs from the commit, every untracked file and every ignored file, `.env` among them
  %%> - removes the tracked files that the checkout deleted, and rewrites the checkout's path in `.env` to `/srv/workspace`
  %%> - checks the exact copied tree inside the container, maps old-checkout targets into the workspace and rewrites absolute internal links there; broken or external links fail with the same code before any Process starts, relative links keep their targets, and source links never change
  %%> - a non-default Instance gets the proxy device that publishes its T3 port
  opt Node runs the main Mailpit
    SW->>C: Apply development mail<br/>Ansible · tags mail
    %%> When:
    %%> - after copying the checkout's `.env`, before application Processes start
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - record `instance.mail_update_failed` for a failed attempt or missing/malformed receipt; application starts, Route cutover and retirement continue, with no rollback for mail; `instance:mail:update` repairs it later
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the shared path status and exact-line result, with line numbers only; conflicts skip the line rule
  end
  SW->>C: Start the container<br/>Processes · T3 · seed
  %%> - container units use `network.target` and nonblocking starts; reads all moved desired-running Processes active with no pending job, waits 5 seconds once for the whole set, then requires each still active with the same positive MainPID and NRestarts; failure names the Process with `instance.migrate_processes_failed` and restores before cutover
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts FrankenPHP and the Instance's existing Processes as `orbit`, with the same ids and desired states; their environment files come through the vault
  %%> - writes the shared FrankenPHP Caddyfile and unit; only the Node's bridge peer with `X-Forwarded-Proto: https` sets PHP's HTTPS scheme, port and resolved client IP; other requests keep native values
  %%> - `vp-dev` uses the runtime folder’s `current/bin/vp`, workspace paths and its assigned port on `0.0.0.0`; only the Node can reach that port, and Caddy sends `/__orbit/vite` there
  %%> - a non-default Instance gets `/etc/orbit/instance`, the agent settings and its T3 server, registered as in create
  %%> - a default Instance gets its first `seed-<commit>` snapshot
  SW->>N: Move the Route<br/>child route-mutation-forward
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - points the Instance's Route at FrankenPHP in the container, and withdraws the checkout's PHP-FPM pool
  alt all steps pass
    SW->>N: Remove the checkout<br/>Ansible · tags retire
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - a due timer fire waits as a recorded Schedule Operation until migration terminal projection reopens admission; its context is rebuilt for the final runtime, on success or rollback
    %%> - every terminal transition settles deferred fires under the Instance lock; closed runtime admission explicitly fails them, including bound start failure and expiry; Schedule settlement preserves the migration result and late native recovery cannot replay a settled fire
    %%> - replaces only the moved Schedules’ checkout-dependent services with host triggers for container execution, keeps their UUID timers and calendars, and resumes each recorded desired state
    %%> - removes the old host Process units and their environment folders
    %%> - repeats the same retirement preflight as an early warning; a new blocker leaves the container serving and the checkout intact
    %%> - atomically moves each old checkout under `<checkout>.orbit-retired-git/<sha256 of original path>`; the retained root is beside the migrating Instance's checkout
    %%> - keeps the whole tree, including Git objects, refs, reflogs, `.git/modules` and nested repositories; a late worktree cannot lose its Git metadata to retirement
    %%> - records `retained_git_path` and `retained_git_at` on the Instance; `instance:show` and the Instance API expose them
    %%> - writes the awake marker; a default's checkout stays until its last worktree has moved; retirement never deletes or prunes Git metadata
    %%> If it fails:
    %%> - the container stays the Instance; the run fails with `instance.migrate_retire_failed`, and the source or retained checkout stays on the Node
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    Note over GW: Record runtime<br/>and Process definitions
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the Instance's workspace is the container's; the runtime runs, a default's row holds its seed commit
    %%> - the same transaction captures each direct moved Process as a Project development definition and links its existing row; known commands use runtime names, opaque guest argv stays exact, and a changed same-name incompatible definition refuses instead of overwriting
    %%> - proven cutover captures definitions even if retirement failed; preflight failures and restored checkout outcomes capture nothing
    %%> - a SQLite file moved with the files, so its connection record goes; stored `.env` values follow the new path
    %%> - the Conn layer records a non-default Instance's T3 server from the result
  else a step fails
    SW->>N: Restore the checkout<br/>Route · container removed
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - puts the Route back on the checkout when the run had moved it
    %%> - deletes the new container, its ACL, its firewall rules and its mirror
    %%> - restores host Process units and the awake marker only when quiesce began; an unreachable target causes zero downtime
    %%> - restores host Schedule timers to their captured activation states; their unit files stay unchanged before cutover
    %%> - the checkout and database remain in place
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step, error_code
    Note over GW: Project native end state
    %%> - showing the Operation or admitting the next migrate settles native moved/restored/ready after expiry; a restored runtime reservation is removed only while this Operation owns it
    %%> - an independent phase failure keeps its code; deadline abort stays failed/`operation.timed_out`, user abort stays cancelled
    %%> - a native finish supplies step statuses and times, even when no events streamed
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again; it starts with a new container
    %%> - a restore that failed keeps the reserved record and its address, and names the failed step
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
